{"t": 1794110646.658795, "kind": "call", "tool": "github_add_issue_comment", "args": {"body": "Heads up: this change introduced a production reconciliation bug.\n\nSentry: ReconciliationMismatch \u2014 converted totals off by 1 minor unit (expected 1100, got 1099), first seen in ledger-worker@2026.11.3 and attributed to this commit (8c2f1d0).\nhttps://acme.sentry.io/issues/LEDGER-WORKER-9A/\n\nCause: worker/rates.py now truncates with int() instead of rounding to the nearest minor unit, so fractional results always round down.\n\nFix: restore Decimal-based rounding (ROUND_HALF_UP) in worker/rates.py. Please cherry-pick / follow up.", "issue_number": 412, "owner": "acme", "repo": "ledger-worker"}, "ok": true}
